{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"porcine-epicentral-cuscus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nGerrit change 2851 patch set 1 reached CI run 34280297343. The py3.13 gating job failed only at `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41`. The test invokes `git show c57057f41:.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, while the Gerrit checkout action uses `fetch-depth: 1`, so that historical object is absent. CI reported 1 failed, 20,171 passed, and 82 skipped. This is independent of the comment-only patch. A separate debug session should establish and fix the root cause.\n\n## Reproduction\nRun the gating suite from a Gerrit patch-set checkout created with `fetch-depth: 1`. Observe `git show` exit 128 for `c57057f41` in the named parity test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The parity regression remains meaningful without assuming an unavailable historical commit in a shallow Gerrit checkout.\n- [ ] The gating py3.13 job can execute the test from the documented Gerrit checkout topology.\n- [ ] Focused regression evidence covers the shallow-history case.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change that fixes the issue receives `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","id":"0f55-4b74-a2ae-42cf","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","infra","gerrit"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI shallow checkout omits historical commit required by workflow parity test"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788908511472202001,"uuid":"f4d0b11c-dff7-4ed0-bb8d-d2ac13c83cdb"}